    {
      "executionState" : "enabled",
      "id" : "note",
      "kind" : "edit.markdownNote",
      "parameters" : {
        "text" : "# Dustdevil Grand Prix · Generated textures\nA pseudo-3D desert rally seen from a chase camera behind your car. Eight cars race three laps on winding, hilly desert roads past cacti, sandstone hoodoos and roadside billboards, with sweeping dust devils on the track. On each Run, one fixed-seed FLUX.2 Klein 4B Distilled job paints the 1024 × 1024 desert panorama behind the road, and five fixed-seed SDXS 512 jobs generate the asphalt, the desert sand, the red sandstone, the weathered wood and the retro billboard poster. Asset Cache stores the six images as named slots for this run and previews each one as it becomes ready. The game starts after all six are ready; later frames reuse the bundle without running either model again. Cancel and Run starts a fresh cache and regenerates all six. Both model packages remain link-only; link the Klein node to the same 4B Distilled package as the bundled Klein example.\n\n**Controls.** The Trackpad is your steering pad; drag in it, or on the full-screen preview. Left and right pick your line across the road: the car steers towards it (the cyan chevron on the road) and holds it. Up and down is the pedal: the upper half is full gas, the band below the middle coasts and the bottom fifth brakes (the pad in the lower-left corner shows the zones and your pointer). Press Action or Space to start, to fire a nitro boost during a race (three per race, plus one for every lap you complete), and to continue from a result screen.\n\n**Goal.** Finish each race in the top three to qualify for the next one. Bends push the car outwards; up to its grip limit the car holds your line by itself, beyond it the car slides wide and scrubs speed, so lift or brake before hard bends and hairpins. Sand slows you down, cacti, hoodoos and billboards beside the road end in a crash, and dust devils shove you sideways. Every finish earns cup points (10, 8, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1); qualify in all three races (Mesa Loop at midday, Rattlesnake Ridge at golden hour, Dustdevil Canyon at dusk) for a gold, silver or bronze trophy. Missing the top three lets you retry the race.\n\n**Settings.** The Game settings JSON sets `laps` (1–5), `rivalPace` (0.8–1.2; lower makes the rivals slower), `nitroPerRace` (0–5) and `firstRace` (1–3). Changing a setting restarts the run."
      },
      "resources" : {

      },
      "title" : "How to play"
    },
